      {
        "id": "E2",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "You can now work through your repository&rsquo;s GitHub code scanning alerts without leaving the GitHub Copilot app.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://github.blog/changelog/2026-10-28-security-extension-for-the-github-copilot-app",
        "source": "GitHub Changelog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-28T15:45:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-29T16:55:08.552Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E3",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The new GitHub security extension, now in public preview, lets you find the alerts that matter most and ask Copilot to explain or help fix them.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://github.blog/changelog/2026-10-28-security-extension-for-the-github-copilot-app",
        "source": "GitHub Changelog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-28T15:45:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-29T16:55:08.552Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E4",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "With the security extension, you can move from finding an alert to fixing it in one place.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://github.blog/changelog/2026-10-28-security-extension-for-the-github-copilot-app",
        "source": "GitHub Changelog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-28T15:45:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-29T16:55:08.552Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "If you already run code scanning on your repository, the security extension shows its open code scanning alerts:",
        "sourceUrl": "https://github.blog/changelog/2026-10-28-security-extension-for-the-github-copilot-app",
        "source": "GitHub Changelog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-28T15:45:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-29T16:55:08.552Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Copilot uses the security extension&rsquo;s tools in the same way as any other tool, following your tool permission settings.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://github.blog/changelog/2026-10-28-security-extension-for-the-github-copilot-app",
        "source": "GitHub Changelog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-28T15:45:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-29T16:55:08.552Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "In the GitHub Copilot app, click Customize , search for github-security , then click + Install .",
        "sourceUrl": "https://github.blog/changelog/2026-10-28-security-extension-for-the-github-copilot-app",
        "source": "GitHub Changelog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-28T15:45:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-29T16:55:08.552Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The security extension is in public preview on github.com and GitHub Enterprise Cloud with data residency.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://github.blog/changelog/2026-10-28-security-extension-for-the-github-copilot-app",
        "source": "GitHub Changelog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-28T15:45:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-29T16:55:08.552Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "With any Copilot plan: You can install the extension and run /security-review on your local changes.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://github.blog/changelog/2026-10-28-security-extension-for-the-github-copilot-app",
        "source": "GitHub Changelog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-28T15:45:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-29T16:55:08.552Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E10",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "For Copilot Business and Copilot Enterprise, an administrator needs to enable the GitHub Copilot app policy, and can use enterprise managed settings to control which plugins developers can install.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://github.blog/changelog/2026-10-28-security-extension-for-the-github-copilot-app",
        "source": "GitHub Changelog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-10-28T15:45:00.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-10-29T16:55:08.552Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E11",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Learn more in the security extension documentation and join the discussion in GitHub Community .",
        "sourceUrl": "https://github.blog/changelog/2026-10-28-security-extension-for-the-github-copilot-app",
        "source": "GitHub Changelog",
